WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.749
Did you have trouble crossing under this bridge
in Chapter 2?

00:00:03.749 --> 00:00:07.749
Well here’s a trick that allows any build to get across:

00:00:07.749 --> 00:00:08.999
Kick-spamming.

00:00:08.999 --> 00:00:11.849
This technique
is useful in so many situations.

00:00:11.849 --> 00:00:13.466
I think this is by far

00:00:13.466 --> 00:00:17.133
the most energy efficient way
to cover a distance in Armored Core 6

00:00:17.216 --> 00:00:18.316
It can save you.

00:00:18.316 --> 00:00:22.616
If you're about to fall off a stage,
it can get you across vast distances.

00:00:22.616 --> 00:00:25.966
It can get you higher than you'd otherwise
be able to go.

00:00:26.033 --> 00:00:30.633
So definitely consider this, especially
if you're equipped with tank treads.

00:00:30.716 --> 00:00:33.599
I think their kick gets you the furthest.

00:00:33.599 --> 00:00:38.116
Speaking of kicks, you might have noticed
that kicks don't just do impact damage.

00:00:38.116 --> 00:00:40.666
They deal direct damage as well.

00:00:40.666 --> 00:00:44.699
And while you might think that leg type
would play a part

00:00:44.699 --> 00:00:48.482
in direct damage or impact dealt,
it doesn't.

00:00:48.566 --> 00:00:52.866
However, the direct damage of your kick
is affected by something.

00:00:52.949 --> 00:00:57.299
It's affected by the weight of your AC,
For example, this is a kick

00:00:57.299 --> 00:01:02.732
with a lightweight AC and here's a kick
with the heaviest tank I could make.

00:01:02.816 --> 00:01:05.866
What's also interesting
is that kicks do roughly three times

00:01:05.866 --> 00:01:08.132
as much damage to enemies
when they're staggered,

00:01:08.132 --> 00:01:12.349
which is a much bigger multiplier
than most other weapons have combined.

00:01:12.349 --> 00:01:15.982
This with the fact that you can spam kicks
pretty fast.

00:01:15.982 --> 00:01:19.849
This can be a really lethal tool,
especially if you have nothing else

00:01:19.849 --> 00:01:21.482
to do while reloading.

00:01:21.482 --> 00:01:25.682
And on some enemies like tetrapod empties,
you can extend

00:01:25.682 --> 00:01:29.349
the duration of their stagger
if you kick them during this state.

00:01:29.432 --> 00:01:34.199
So if you haven't worked kicks into your
playstyle yet, absolutely do that.

00:01:34.282 --> 00:01:35.215
But let's be honest.

00:01:35.215 --> 00:01:37.499
More important
than anything else in this video

00:01:37.499 --> 00:01:41.348
is your fashion,
your armor decor, so to speak.

00:01:41.432 --> 00:01:45.698
And one key part of your fashion
is your booster color,

00:01:45.782 --> 00:01:49.548
because did you notice that booster color
isn't determined by the booster part.

00:01:49.548 --> 00:01:52.932
Instead, it's
actually determined by your generator.

00:01:52.998 --> 00:01:55.398
For example,
this generator gives me a blue booster,

00:01:55.398 --> 00:01:59.582
which actually turns
my gold AC like an ugly green.

00:01:59.665 --> 00:02:02.598
This one gives a nice default orange,
which is better.

00:02:02.598 --> 00:02:06.082
But this coral generator gives me this
awesome red color.

00:02:06.332 --> 00:02:10.598
And even though it has a recharge delay
of like 5 seconds,

00:02:10.682 --> 00:02:12.598
you know, I'm still going to use it.

00:02:12.598 --> 00:02:16.465
Speaking of fashion, though,
this is my LG Corporation, AC

00:02:16.648 --> 00:02:22.448
and I made this because LG are actually
our corporate sponsor for this video.

00:02:22.531 --> 00:02:27.031
So I wanted to do a video with LG
because uniquely among Fromsoftware

00:02:27.031 --> 00:02:31.831
games, Armored Core 6
actually has amazing widescreen support.

00:02:31.915 --> 00:02:34.765
So LG sent over one of their ultrawides
for me

00:02:34.765 --> 00:02:37.798
to show you guys,
and I was absolutely blown away.

00:02:37.831 --> 00:02:42.781
This, I think, is unironically the best
way to play Armored Core, in my opinion.

00:02:42.865 --> 00:02:46.781
The curved screen just makes this game
so immersive,

00:02:46.848 --> 00:02:50.364
and having a wide field of view
is legitimately incredible

00:02:50.364 --> 00:02:52.948
for your situational awareness
because you can see

00:02:52.948 --> 00:02:55.498
all of the enemies around you
while you're fighting.

00:02:55.498 --> 00:03:00.198
So this is the LG Ultra Gear OLED 45GR95QE

00:03:00.231 --> 00:03:04.048
Sounds like it could be a part in game.

00:03:04.131 --> 00:03:06.898
It's a 45 inch 21 by nine

00:03:06.898 --> 00:03:12.481
display with a clean, really
borderless design and also a crazy fast

00:03:12.481 --> 00:03:17.848
0.03 millisecond response time,
which makes it perfect for gaming.

00:03:18.081 --> 00:03:20.847
The also touting this as the world's

00:03:20.847 --> 00:03:24.297
first 240 hertz gaming monitor.

00:03:24.381 --> 00:03:25.547
If you're interested in

00:03:25.547 --> 00:03:29.247
investing in one for yourself,
check out the link in the description.

00:03:29.331 --> 00:03:33.364
And thank you to LG
for sponsoring this video number five.

00:03:33.447 --> 00:03:37.497
If you ever run out of energy in the air,
you are extremely vulnerable.

00:03:37.497 --> 00:03:40.781
You can't dodge or fly
or you can do is fall.

00:03:40.847 --> 00:03:43.947
But did you know that
falling directly down

00:03:43.947 --> 00:03:46.981
is actually the best thing you can do
in this situation?

00:03:46.981 --> 00:03:48.264
A lot of the time

00:03:48.264 --> 00:03:50.597
when you push forward on the left
analog stick,

00:03:50.597 --> 00:03:53.730
as long as your boosters are toggled
on, you'll still float

00:03:53.730 --> 00:03:56.930
somewhat horizontally,
even when you're completely out of energy.

00:03:57.114 --> 00:03:59.747
Note our speed while we're doing this.

00:03:59.747 --> 00:04:02.747
However, if you let go of the left, stick
completely,

00:04:02.880 --> 00:04:06.730
your boosters will deactivate
and you'll end to freefall mode.

00:04:06.797 --> 00:04:10.230
In this state, you'll fall a lot faster,
even though

00:04:10.230 --> 00:04:14.047
it says your boosters are still on
just look at the speed difference.

00:04:14.130 --> 00:04:17.480
Therefore, free falling straight down
can actually make

00:04:17.480 --> 00:04:21.147
you way more avoidant of projectiles
coming your way,

00:04:21.230 --> 00:04:25.947
especially if you're falling perpendicular
to the shot that's coming your way.

00:04:26.030 --> 00:04:28.547
So consider doing this as a last resort.

00:04:28.547 --> 00:04:32.380
Next time you run out of energy. 
Number 6:

00:04:32.447 --> 00:04:35.097
So target assist can be great.

00:04:35.097 --> 00:04:38.397
It gives you unparalleled
focus on single enemies

00:04:38.397 --> 00:04:42.330
and it makes it way easier for you
to focus on dodging and flying.

00:04:42.413 --> 00:04:46.030
But it's actually not
the optimal way to play.

00:04:46.097 --> 00:04:50.847
That's because when you toggle on target
assist, your tracking strength is actually

00:04:50.847 --> 00:04:55.830
compromised and less of your shots
will find their mark as a result.

00:04:55.913 --> 00:04:58.913
This is absolutely something
you can feel in the gameplay

00:04:59.147 --> 00:05:02.330
and you might have even noticed
how much more your reticle

00:05:02.446 --> 00:05:05.363
lags behind
when you're locked on in this way.

00:05:05.363 --> 00:05:08.480
But the question is
how bad is this effect?

00:05:08.480 --> 00:05:13.180
How much is your tracking strength
compromised when using target assist?

00:05:13.246 --> 00:05:14.663
Let's try to figure it out.

00:05:14.663 --> 00:05:19.796
So there are a lot of variables that make
this really hard to test in a vacuum.

00:05:19.880 --> 00:05:23.813
We have to ensure that our enemy is moving
in pretty much the exact

00:05:23.813 --> 00:05:27.963
same way at the exact
same speed, at the exact same distance

00:05:28.046 --> 00:05:30.930
with target assist toggled on
and then off.

00:05:30.930 --> 00:05:32.880
So I came up with this.

00:05:32.880 --> 00:05:37.829
The jump test. With this, distance
and movement become controlled variables

00:05:37.829 --> 00:05:41.363
and we can really try to narrow
down the difference in accuracy

00:05:41.546 --> 00:05:44.546
with target assist toggled on and off.

00:05:44.629 --> 00:05:45.946
Here's what I found.

00:05:45.946 --> 00:05:48.529
So at 50 meters with target assist

00:05:48.529 --> 00:05:52.446
of 0.018% of my shots missed

00:05:52.529 --> 00:05:57.063
compared to 12% of my shots
missing with target assist

00:05:57.146 --> 00:06:02.229
at 100 meters with target assist off
27% of my shots missed

00:06:02.296 --> 00:06:05.763
compared to 47% with target assist

00:06:05.846 --> 00:06:09.996
and at 150 meters with target assist off,
it was 44%

00:06:10.079 --> 00:06:13.012
compared to 61% with target assist.

00:06:13.012 --> 00:06:16.796
And then at 200 meters, 55% of my shots
missed without it

00:06:16.879 --> 00:06:20.212
and 74% missed with target assist.

00:06:20.362 --> 00:06:23.479
So just at a glance from that data,

00:06:23.596 --> 00:06:26.846
target assist is clearly having
a big impact here.

00:06:26.929 --> 00:06:33.062
In many cases, almost twice as many of my
shots missed while using target assist.

00:06:33.146 --> 00:06:36.562
Now, admittedly,
I didn't get like a huge sample size here

00:06:36.562 --> 00:06:40.862
and I only tested this with one weapon,
so I'd really like to invite someone

00:06:40.862 --> 00:06:44.045
better than me to perform
the jump test more thoroughly.

00:06:44.129 --> 00:06:47.329
If I find someone who does
a really good experiment online, I'll

00:06:47.545 --> 00:06:49.829
pin their results in the comments
section below.

00:06:49.829 --> 00:06:51.862
But for now, I think it's safe to say that

00:06:51.862 --> 00:06:55.779
you really should be trying to learn
to play without target assist if you can,

00:06:55.862 --> 00:06:59.495
especially if your enemy is small
and agile.

00:06:59.579 --> 00:07:02.579
For number seven,
let's talk about these gaps

00:07:02.662 --> 00:07:06.212
So often advice
I give when building an AC is

00:07:06.212 --> 00:07:10.212
to try and stay as close
to your maximum loads as possible.

00:07:10.279 --> 00:07:13.279
This will ensure that you're packing
on the most value

00:07:13.312 --> 00:07:16.528
that your legs and generator can support.

00:07:16.612 --> 00:07:19.195
That said,
there are benefits to leaving gaps here

00:07:19.195 --> 00:07:22.378
that you might not know about in regards
to your maximum load.

00:07:22.412 --> 00:07:25.945
A larger gap
will contribute towards your boost speed.

00:07:26.162 --> 00:07:30.412
So notice how my boost speed becomes
faster when I just unequipped my weapons.

00:07:30.445 --> 00:07:33.712
That's because leftover load
contributes to your speed.

00:07:33.895 --> 00:07:37.578
You can even achieve this boost
to your speed by purging weapons

00:07:37.578 --> 00:07:38.845
during a mission.

00:07:38.845 --> 00:07:42.662
What's interesting is that a similar logic
applies to your EN load as well.

00:07:42.745 --> 00:07:46.445
The larger the gap, the faster
your energy bar will recharge.

00:07:46.528 --> 00:07:47.995
That's because leftover

00:07:47.995 --> 00:07:52.445
EN output contributes
towards your supply efficiency stat.

00:07:52.528 --> 00:07:55.911
The higher this value, the faster
your energy bar will move

00:07:56.161 --> 00:07:57.745
after the recharge delay.

00:07:57.745 --> 00:08:00.295
Just look at this difference now.

00:08:00.295 --> 00:08:04.378
It's really cool that the game rewards
your excess like this,

00:08:04.461 --> 00:08:08.495
but I will say in my experience,
the benefits of having a large gap

00:08:08.578 --> 00:08:13.411
still don't really outweigh the benefits
of just stacking on better parts instead.

00:08:13.495 --> 00:08:16.128
For example,
your energy is coming back fast

00:08:16.128 --> 00:08:20.528
either way, you know,
but it's a nice thing to have for sure.

00:08:20.611 --> 00:08:24.828
Another thing that's really nice to have
is the hanger bay upgrade in your own

00:08:24.861 --> 00:08:26.028
tuning screen.

00:08:26.028 --> 00:08:29.911
This allows you to store
two more arm parts on your back.

00:08:29.994 --> 00:08:32.661
Note,
however, that you can't fire these weapons

00:08:32.661 --> 00:08:34.311
when they're stored in the hanger.

00:08:34.311 --> 00:08:39.544
Instead, L1 and R1 will just switch
to these weapons for your arms instead.

00:08:39.628 --> 00:08:42.378
And when you first think about it,
that seems kind of bad, right?

00:08:42.378 --> 00:08:45.394
After all, wouldn't you just want to fire
four weapons at once?

00:08:45.411 --> 00:08:48.411
Isn't that more DPS than just two?

00:08:48.411 --> 00:08:54.027
However, consider this weapons
that overheat can cool down in the hanger.

00:08:54.111 --> 00:08:57.311
Weapons can even reload
while they're in the hanger.

00:08:57.377 --> 00:08:59.661
So just think about how good that is.

00:08:59.661 --> 00:09:00.827
With this technique,

00:09:00.827 --> 00:09:05.527
you can offset the downside of some of
the strongest weapons in the game.

00:09:05.611 --> 00:09:09.477
Fire your chain guns to overheat
and then switch to shotguns

00:09:09.477 --> 00:09:11.544
while they cool down in the hanger.

00:09:11.544 --> 00:09:14.877
Break guards with the pile bunker
melee weapon, then

00:09:15.111 --> 00:09:18.911
pull out a sword to capitalize on that
while it cools down.

00:09:18.977 --> 00:09:22.961
Or just equip four machine guns and switch
them out whenever you need to reload.

00:09:23.027 --> 00:09:26.877
This way
your DPS is absolutely unrelenting,

00:09:26.877 --> 00:09:30.960
and I unironically think after
testing a lot of this stuff that hang

00:09:31.010 --> 00:09:35.494
builds will end up being
some of the strongest builds in the game.

00:09:35.577 --> 00:09:38.027
Anyway, speaking of OS upgrades,

00:09:38.027 --> 00:09:41.460
do you regret any of the OS upgrades
you've invested in?

00:09:41.544 --> 00:09:45.327
Well, don't worry, because by
pressing triangle or Y in this menu

00:09:45.560 --> 00:09:49.360
you can undo each upgrade
you've purchased for 4000 credits.

00:09:49.427 --> 00:09:52.827
One reason I did my points
is because I realized that

00:09:53.060 --> 00:09:56.610
the most efficient way to invest
your points is actually to invest

00:09:56.610 --> 00:10:02.260
in the lowest tier of many upgrades
rather than going deep into just one.

00:10:02.327 --> 00:10:05.210
That's
because the lowest tiers are the cheapest.

00:10:05.210 --> 00:10:09.210
So it's kind of best
to buy all the low tiers first.

00:10:09.293 --> 00:10:10.110
Number ten.

00:10:10.110 --> 00:10:14.310
This next trick is particularly good
when you're fighting an enemy AC.

00:10:14.393 --> 00:10:16.110
Though I'll admit it's a pretty high

00:10:16.110 --> 00:10:19.960
skill cap thing to do,
and that's melee canceling.

00:10:20.027 --> 00:10:23.610
So by tapping quick boost
right at the end of your melee boost,

00:10:23.810 --> 00:10:28.193
you're able to cancel your melee boost
and immediately initiated again,

00:10:28.410 --> 00:10:32.093
creating a loop
where you're constantly moving, closing

00:10:32.093 --> 00:10:34.343
in on and threatening the enemy.

00:10:34.343 --> 00:10:37.343
AC Without even overheating your weapon.

00:10:37.560 --> 00:10:40.076
This is particularly good
if you've chosen a booster

00:10:40.076 --> 00:10:45.410
that has a really good melee attack
thrust and a melee attack in consumption

00:10:45.410 --> 00:10:48.893
spec, as these can enable you
to close the gap

00:10:48.893 --> 00:10:52.660
between enemies more effectively
than even an assault boost could.

00:10:52.726 --> 00:10:54.510
It also looks cool as hell.

00:10:54.510 --> 00:10:57.510
That's kind of the main reason
to do this, honestly.

00:10:57.560 --> 00:11:02.043
But the coolest thing you can do
in Armored Core is s-ranking missions

00:11:02.126 --> 00:11:04.943
according to the game
to achieve an S rank rating.

00:11:04.943 --> 00:11:07.943
You must complete the mission
without retrying from a checkpoint

00:11:07.976 --> 00:11:13.559
while also minimizing incoming damage,
time taken and ammunition consumed.

00:11:13.643 --> 00:11:16.126
In practice, though,
it's actually not that simple.

00:11:16.126 --> 00:11:19.743
For example, in the mission, destroy
the transport helicopters.

00:11:19.826 --> 00:11:23.859
I finished the objectives extremely fast
without taking a point of damage

00:11:23.926 --> 00:11:26.876
and only got an eight rank to achieve an S
rank.

00:11:26.876 --> 00:11:31.593
I realized it helped a lot
to actually kill some enemies as well.

00:11:31.676 --> 00:11:32.726
The game doesn't tell you

00:11:32.726 --> 00:11:36.359
that you need to kill enemies,
but that is important apparently.

00:11:36.443 --> 00:11:39.859
And then for certain missions
it seems like the s rank criteria are

00:11:39.859 --> 00:11:41.126
weighted differently.

00:11:41.126 --> 00:11:44.992
For example, in a chapter two mission,
I destroyed the smart cleaner

00:11:44.992 --> 00:11:48.426
very quickly,
but I used dual Gatling guns to do it.

00:11:48.509 --> 00:11:53.076
And even though I didn't die, I achieved
a really low rank for some reason

00:11:53.159 --> 00:11:57.276
for this mission, it seems ammunition
cost counted against me greatly.

00:11:57.359 --> 00:12:00.209
And then there was this mission
where I took a ton of damage,

00:12:00.209 --> 00:12:02.176
and I was sure that I did terribly.

00:12:02.176 --> 00:12:03.709
And then I got an AC rank.

00:12:03.709 --> 00:12:08.376
Turns out this mission has an extremely
high tolerance for the damage you take.

00:12:08.459 --> 00:12:12.292
So my takeaway from all of this
is that while it's certainly possible

00:12:12.292 --> 00:12:16.859
to s rank by focusing on
just doing one thing, well,

00:12:16.942 --> 00:12:20.242
there are missions where it feels like
some things matter more than most.

00:12:20.425 --> 00:12:24.042
So definitely
try and switch up your build and strategy

00:12:24.059 --> 00:12:25.975
if you're not having much success.

00:12:25.975 --> 00:12:28.709
Build for speed or kills or low ammunition

00:12:28.709 --> 00:12:32.092
cost or low damage
taken and see how you go.

00:12:32.092 --> 00:12:34.225
Prioritizing different things.

00:12:34.225 --> 00:12:37.409
But what's the reward for ranking
every mission in the game, you ask?

00:12:37.492 --> 00:12:39.692
Well, it makes you feel good.

00:12:39.692 --> 00:12:45.209
According to my review guide, you get a
trophy and an achievement and that's it.

00:12:45.292 --> 00:12:47.842
Which I'll admit
is a little bit disappointing.

00:12:47.842 --> 00:12:50.842
I wish there was some incentive, but

00:12:50.992 --> 00:12:53.842
I guess it's
more about the journey in the end.

00:12:53.842 --> 00:12:56.308
One of the metrics for s ranking missions

00:12:56.308 --> 00:12:59.458
is, again,
not being wasteful with your ammunition.

00:12:59.658 --> 00:13:03.992
So you might think that reloading manually
and just throwing away

00:13:03.992 --> 00:13:08.008
the entire rest of the magazine
would be wasteful, right?

00:13:08.092 --> 00:13:08.642
Wrong.

00:13:08.642 --> 00:13:11.342
Because video game
laws are in effect here.

00:13:11.342 --> 00:13:15.325
And when you reload an armored core six,
your magazine will magically

00:13:15.325 --> 00:13:18.325
fill with the exact amount of ammunition
you need.

00:13:18.408 --> 00:13:21.408
Despite
that kind of being physically impossible,

00:13:21.475 --> 00:13:24.141
that means that you only really need
to worry about

00:13:24.141 --> 00:13:28.025
the ammunition that you fire in a mission
and nothing more.

00:13:28.108 --> 00:13:32.491
Being wasteful is a pretty fast way
to rack up some debt in armored core six.

00:13:32.491 --> 00:13:36.058
Though
admittedly, incurring debt is quite rare.

00:13:36.208 --> 00:13:39.208
Even if you're firing
the most expensive weaponry.

00:13:39.325 --> 00:13:41.491
This is the most debt I could get
when I tried.

00:13:41.491 --> 00:13:42.591
For example.

00:13:42.591 --> 00:13:46.441
I just quickly wanted to confirm
that yeah, it is possible to go negative

00:13:46.441 --> 00:13:51.008
in the mission and lose money, though
no matter how much you waste or lose,

00:13:51.091 --> 00:13:56.908
it's impossible to actually go negative in
terms of your total funds in the garage.

00:13:56.991 --> 00:13:58.791
Speaking of firing ammunition,

00:13:58.791 --> 00:14:02.208
there are many situations
where you might want to consider

00:14:02.208 --> 00:14:06.158
staggering your fire
rather than unloading all at once.

00:14:06.241 --> 00:14:09.724
For example, when fighting a fast opponent
like an enemy AC,

00:14:09.808 --> 00:14:13.491
it's very likely that they'll dodge
your attacks, especially your missiles.

00:14:13.524 --> 00:14:17.491
So for example, if you unload
two sets of missiles at them at once,

00:14:17.574 --> 00:14:21.724
they can just easily negate
both of those salvos with one dodge.

00:14:21.808 --> 00:14:26.791
Instead, what you should do is fire
one after the other with a short delay.

00:14:26.874 --> 00:14:29.957
This way you're far more likely
to catch them during or

00:14:30.207 --> 00:14:33.791
after a dodge
with at least one set of missiles.

00:14:33.857 --> 00:14:36.441
The same applies to weapons with a slow
firing rate.

00:14:36.441 --> 00:14:39.207
Take dual shotguns, for example.

00:14:39.207 --> 00:14:42.391
If I fire both at once,
they're both liable to miss.

00:14:42.391 --> 00:14:46.291
But if I fire one after the other,
even if I miss one,

00:14:46.491 --> 00:14:49.407
the second is far more likely to connect.

00:14:49.407 --> 00:14:52.107
Spacing out
your shots also makes it less likely

00:14:52.107 --> 00:14:56.091
that enemies will get a chance
to recover their ACS build up,

00:14:56.207 --> 00:15:00.757
which is what can happen
if they go too long without taking damage.

00:15:00.840 --> 00:15:05.307
Next, I believe that there are just
two status effects in Armored Core 6: 

00:15:05.390 --> 00:15:08.640
ACS anomaly and electrical discharge.

00:15:08.840 --> 00:15:13.257
However, the game doesn't really explain
what these are, so I'll try.

00:15:13.340 --> 00:15:17.007
ACS anomaly is built up over time with fire
based attacks.

00:15:17.240 --> 00:15:18.740
When the bar fills completely,

00:15:18.740 --> 00:15:22.057
you'll receive this warning,
which lasts for about 10 seconds.

00:15:22.140 --> 00:15:27.607
During this time, the impact damage
you receive is significantly increased.

00:15:27.690 --> 00:15:30.540
Compare this, for example,

00:15:30.624 --> 00:15:33.090
to this.

00:15:33.090 --> 00:15:36.173
And while we're looking at the staggered
gauge, it's important to note

00:15:36.173 --> 00:15:40.157
that the metal bar is easier to fill up
than the outer bars.

00:15:40.257 --> 00:15:44.240
Essentially, it seems like this middle
section counts as one bar

00:15:44.457 --> 00:15:47.907
and filling
the outer two bars takes twice as long.

00:15:48.140 --> 00:15:52.140
There are two bars on the outside
after all, so effectively

00:15:52.140 --> 00:15:55.307
it seems like ACS anomaly increases
the impact

00:15:55.307 --> 00:15:59.090
damage
you take by about 50% for 10 seconds,

00:15:59.090 --> 00:16:03.457
which makes it really quite
an impactful status effect.

00:16:03.540 --> 00:16:07.823
The other status effect in AC
six is the shock status effect,

00:16:07.823 --> 00:16:13.056
which I figured out is essentially bleed
from other from soft games.

00:16:13.140 --> 00:16:14.690
Basically what happens is

00:16:14.690 --> 00:16:19.673
when you take electrical damage,
your elec discharge bar will fill doing

00:16:19.673 --> 00:16:24.390
a burst of damage once at the end
when the bar is completely filled.

00:16:24.473 --> 00:16:27.840
What's interesting about this
shock effects in this game, though, is

00:16:27.840 --> 00:16:33.656
that it's actually not percentage based
damage unlike bleed from previous games.

00:16:33.740 --> 00:16:37.890
Regardless of your AP,
this effect seems to do a flat

00:16:37.890 --> 00:16:42.839
1600 damage,
meaning shock will kind of naturally

00:16:42.839 --> 00:16:47.106
be better against lightweight aces
rather than heavy ones.

00:16:47.189 --> 00:16:51.006
Of course, you can build up status effects
on other enemies as well,

00:16:51.089 --> 00:16:54.339
even non AC enemies like MT’s.

00:16:54.406 --> 00:16:58.456
Though it's worth noting that clearly
some enemies have more resistance

00:16:58.523 --> 00:17:04.439
than others and some bosses effectively
seem immune to status effects entirely.

00:17:04.523 --> 00:17:09.423
Now that kind of is a third status effect,
although it's strictly not one as well.

00:17:09.506 --> 00:17:12.023
It's the smoke bomb, which has an effect

00:17:12.023 --> 00:17:15.739
that creates a little bubble,
a little zone.

00:17:15.739 --> 00:17:20.189
And while you're inside this zone,
you can't lock on to enemies outside it

00:17:20.389 --> 00:17:23.889
and they can't lock on to you
if you're inside it either.

00:17:23.956 --> 00:17:28.406
However, if you're both inside the zone,
then you can lock onto each other.

00:17:28.489 --> 00:17:31.906
And if the smoke is in between
both of you, it actually acts

00:17:31.906 --> 00:17:33.106
like a piece of terrain.

00:17:33.106 --> 00:17:37.556
Would it blocks you from locking onto
the enemy at a distance as well?

00:17:37.639 --> 00:17:41.689
Essentially, this is really cool,
but as its description states,

00:17:41.939 --> 00:17:46.922
it's going to take a lot of finesse
to effectively use this in combat.

00:17:47.005 --> 00:17:50.489
If there are more status effects
in the game I haven't listed, I apologize.

00:17:50.522 --> 00:17:52.889
I'm playing through the game
really thoroughly,

00:17:52.889 --> 00:17:55.489
but I'm playing through
really slowly as well.

00:17:55.489 --> 00:17:58.889
I've only just finished chapter three,
so it's possible that there's more

00:17:58.922 --> 00:18:00.139
that I'm missing.

00:18:00.139 --> 00:18:04.639
Number 16 canceling this is only mentioned
very briefly in training.

00:18:04.639 --> 00:18:10.239
So remember pressing triangle or Y
will allow you to cancel certain actions.

00:18:10.322 --> 00:18:13.072
For example,
if you're charging a weapon and no longer

00:18:13.072 --> 00:18:16.072
want to charge it,
just press triangle or Y.

00:18:16.139 --> 00:18:19.022
And if you've started a multi lock
that you regret, you can also

00:18:19.022 --> 00:18:22.888
press triangle
or Y to revert to a single lock.

00:18:22.972 --> 00:18:27.422
Now, I'm kind of shocked that this next
tip isn't in the official tutorial,

00:18:27.505 --> 00:18:32.872
and that's that in most situations it's
not optimal to cancel your assault boost

00:18:33.088 --> 00:18:37.272
by pulling back on the left
stick like the tutorial tells you to do.

00:18:37.338 --> 00:18:40.288
Doing this
actually brings you to an abrupt halt,

00:18:40.288 --> 00:18:44.005
which can easily get
you killed instead, by pushing forward

00:18:44.005 --> 00:18:47.355
on the left stick
and just tapping the send button.

00:18:47.438 --> 00:18:50.988
You're able to cancel your assault, boost
and maintain

00:18:50.988 --> 00:18:54.988
your forward momentum,
which is just objectively better.

00:18:55.071 --> 00:18:56.238
Number 18.

00:18:56.238 --> 00:18:58.171
So unlike in other from soft games,

00:18:58.171 --> 00:19:01.588
you can't actually load
multiple saves in the main menu.

00:19:01.671 --> 00:19:05.071
You can only have one playthrough
active at any time.

00:19:05.071 --> 00:19:07.221
So be careful of that new game

00:19:07.221 --> 00:19:11.021
button this time around
since it will overwrite your current safe.

00:19:11.088 --> 00:19:12.955
I can kind of see why they made it
this way.

00:19:12.955 --> 00:19:14.755
The game is designed around

00:19:14.755 --> 00:19:18.521
replaying missions and going into new game
plus after all.

00:19:18.588 --> 00:19:21.838
One thing that oddly does seem to persist
if you start

00:19:21.838 --> 00:19:25.771
a new game is your AC data
from your previous save.

00:19:25.855 --> 00:19:28.771
If you didn't know in this menu,
you can quickly build

00:19:28.771 --> 00:19:34.721
your old saved AC designs though
of course you still need their parts.

00:19:34.788 --> 00:19:36.171
I'd also quickly like to mention

00:19:36.171 --> 00:19:39.754
that you can upload your AC designs
in this menu as well.

00:19:39.838 --> 00:19:44.454
This will give you a code to share with
others who might want to create your AC.

00:19:44.671 --> 00:19:49.988
Here's the code for my LG AC though
this doesn't seem to work cross-platform.

00:19:50.071 --> 00:19:54.088
The same goes for Emblem Designs
while you're in the garage.

00:19:54.121 --> 00:19:58.988
One thing not many people realize you can
do is enter photo mode while you're here.

00:19:59.071 --> 00:20:02.304
Here you can fly your camera around
quite far

00:20:02.304 --> 00:20:06.321
and explore the little container
that you're a stowaway within.

00:20:06.571 --> 00:20:10.437
And of course, the same photo mode can be
activated while you're out on a mission

00:20:10.437 --> 00:20:12.171
during the pause menu.

00:20:12.171 --> 00:20:14.787
Another small thing,
but there are situations

00:20:14.787 --> 00:20:19.171
where you really should use the compass
and the radar that's built into it.

00:20:19.254 --> 00:20:22.621
In this mission, for example, it's
important for me to head towards enemies

00:20:22.621 --> 00:20:27.154
as soon as they appear and my radar
is the best way of doing that.

00:20:27.237 --> 00:20:27.921
What's more,

00:20:27.921 --> 00:20:32.621
lots of information shows up down
here, like target objectives and more.

00:20:32.687 --> 00:20:35.637
These little arrows for example,
also indicate

00:20:35.637 --> 00:20:39.904
if an enemy is above or below
you in that direction.

00:20:39.987 --> 00:20:43.170
If you're on your first attempt
or don't care at all about

00:20:43.337 --> 00:20:46.637
ranking a mission, consider
simply restarting from check points

00:20:46.637 --> 00:20:48.887
as soon as you notice
that you've reached one.

00:20:48.887 --> 00:20:52.320
For example, here
I've taken so much damage that there's

00:20:52.320 --> 00:20:56.320
just no way I'm going to beat Sula
in this upcoming fight.

00:20:56.387 --> 00:20:58.337
It would be a waste of my time.

00:20:58.337 --> 00:21:02.187
Instead, as soon as I noticed
this indicator in the bottom right,

00:21:02.270 --> 00:21:06.387
I can just manually start
from the checkpoint and fully restore

00:21:06.387 --> 00:21:10.037
my AP 
and my repair packets. For number 22,

00:21:10.070 --> 00:21:16.353
Remember that your standard repair
kit heals a flat 4000 AP So when healing,

00:21:16.437 --> 00:21:19.920
try to make sure that you've taken
4000 damage before healing it.

00:21:20.087 --> 00:21:23.720
And when building an AC,
consider that you functionally have

00:21:23.937 --> 00:21:28.170
12,000 more
AP than what it's showing you on screen.

00:21:28.253 --> 00:21:33.370
So when you think about your functional
AP and keep healing in mind

00:21:33.437 --> 00:21:37.053
the difference between a heavyweight
AC with a lot of AP

00:21:37.137 --> 00:21:41.036
and a lightweight
AC with not much AP, the difference

00:21:41.036 --> 00:21:43.703
between them gets smaller
when you take into account

00:21:43.703 --> 00:21:48.670
that both builds have 12,000
HP on top of what they already have.

00:21:48.736 --> 00:21:51.836
That said, repair kits
aren't a thing in the arena,

00:21:51.920 --> 00:21:55.786
so I think that heavy ACS really
will benefit

00:21:55.786 --> 00:21:59.753
from their raw AP and defensive stats
a lot more.

00:21:59.786 --> 00:22:04.586
They're just one extra thing when you fall
off the map in armored classics.

00:22:04.670 --> 00:22:07.403
You don't take a flat AP punishment.

00:22:07.403 --> 00:22:12.370
Instead, falling off
the map will take 35% of your total AP.

00:22:12.436 --> 00:22:16.136
Let's talk about some of the lesser used
OS tuning upgrades.

00:22:16.219 --> 00:22:19.853
One of the worst kind of has to be access
speed optimization,

00:22:19.853 --> 00:22:24.986
which increases your interaction
speed by 50% and then 100%.

00:22:25.069 --> 00:22:28.036
This can be useful,
but it's extremely situational.

00:22:28.036 --> 00:22:28.936
For example,

00:22:28.936 --> 00:22:32.453
some missions might have you hack
something while you're in firing range.

00:22:32.453 --> 00:22:34.069
It's pretty good then.

00:22:34.069 --> 00:22:38.686
So I'd definitely consider this upgrade
to be great for ranking certain missions,

00:22:38.686 --> 00:22:43.086
but other than that,
I rank it as a pretty low priority.

00:22:43.169 --> 00:22:46.069
One little secret you might have missed
with this, though, is that

00:22:46.069 --> 00:22:49.652
objects have different
scan levels associated with them.

00:22:49.736 --> 00:22:55.652
I've found three scan levels so far,
and the higher that they're stored LV is,

00:22:55.736 --> 00:23:01.519
the longer they will take to access
another arguably less important OS tuning

00:23:01.519 --> 00:23:05.119
upgrade is the quick turn,
which when unlocked, allows you

00:23:05.119 --> 00:23:10.186
to do a 90 degree or a 180 degree
turn of your mic and the camera

00:23:10.336 --> 00:23:16.119
by holding circle or B and turning
your left stick in the desired direction.

00:23:16.186 --> 00:23:19.186
In any other Armored Core game,
this would be incredible.

00:23:19.319 --> 00:23:23.052
But in Armored Core 6  it's
kind of just all right.

00:23:23.119 --> 00:23:26.585
The best thing about it is that it moves
your camera faster than you can.

00:23:26.669 --> 00:23:29.602
Even with camera speeds
set to ten, though,

00:23:29.602 --> 00:23:33.635
those playing with mouse and keyboard
actually won't have this problem at all.

00:23:33.719 --> 00:23:36.685
It's worth unlocking this
if you play with a controller

00:23:36.685 --> 00:23:38.852
and if you play without target assist.

00:23:38.852 --> 00:23:43.419
But I feel like most players
can confidently give this one a miss.

00:23:43.502 --> 00:23:46.369
Another very neat OS
upgrade is weight control,

00:23:46.369 --> 00:23:51.119
which lets you enter missions overweight
and manually purge your weapons.

00:23:51.202 --> 00:23:54.385
Being over your weight
limit seems to penalize your speed

00:23:54.385 --> 00:23:58.585
in a similar way to how being under
your weight limit rewards your speed.

00:23:58.668 --> 00:24:02.968
So going into a mission overweight
really isn't the worst thing in the world.

00:24:03.052 --> 00:24:06.002
The best use case I could think of for
this would be

00:24:06.002 --> 00:24:09.968
when you use it in tandem
with its manual purge function.

00:24:10.052 --> 00:24:12.718
This way you could enter a mission
with heavy weaponry.

00:24:12.718 --> 00:24:15.602
You could use up those weapons
and then you could purge them

00:24:15.602 --> 00:24:17.635
if you no longer have a use for them.

00:24:17.635 --> 00:24:22.418
So the best use case I could think of for
that was to bring in heavy snipers.

00:24:22.502 --> 00:24:25.918
Use them at a safe range where
your lack of speed doesn't really matter.

00:24:26.002 --> 00:24:29.368
Then purge them and get in close
with your faster AC.

00:24:29.451 --> 00:24:32.185
What's also cool is that you'll
get these weapons back after

00:24:32.185 --> 00:24:36.985
you've purged them at a resupply station,
so you will be able to have them back

00:24:36.985 --> 00:24:40.718
for difficult boss encounters
at the end of the mission.

00:24:40.801 --> 00:24:43.168
And if you do go with this purging
strategy,

00:24:43.168 --> 00:24:47.401
consider choosing an arm part
with a high melee specialization step.

00:24:47.485 --> 00:24:51.118
This will increase the damage
of your punches, but so far for me,

00:24:51.151 --> 00:24:55.751
haven't really been able to build around
weight control in a meaningful way.

00:24:55.818 --> 00:24:59.068
Maybe later in the game I'll unlock
some parts that make that viable.

00:24:59.118 --> 00:25:02.618
So I'm curious
if you guys have any ideas for that.

00:25:02.701 --> 00:25:04.351
But that's it.

00:25:04.351 --> 00:25:08.668
Before I go again, think about investing
in an ultrawide monitor for your setup.

00:25:08.784 --> 00:25:11.784
It's so good. Links in the description.

00:25:11.868 --> 00:25:14.601
Thanks again
to LG for sponsoring this video.

00:25:14.601 --> 00:25:15.384
Forget BALAM

00:25:15.384 --> 00:25:16.651
Forget ARQUEBUS

00:25:16.651 --> 00:25:17.251
Thank you.

00:25:17.251 --> 00:25:19.551
LG and I'll see you all next time.

